Subject: [PATCH 09/13] port: DSPARK/DFLASH return_logprob via
 compute_spec_v2_logprobs

RL rollouts need sampled-token logprobs (MIS/TIS); upstream hard-blocked
them under DSPARK/DFLASH. The scheduler/result pipeline is already generic
for spec-v2 logprobs; ngram_worker.py:457 is the chain-verifier precedent.

- validate_dflash_request: drop the return_logprob rejection.
- dspark_worker_v2/dflash_worker_v2: drop the raises; at accept-branch
  convergence synthesize the chain accept_index (committed token j of
  request i <- verify row i*W+j, -1 past commit_lens; padded rows unread
  downstream) and call compute_spec_v2_logprobs(batch, logits_output,
  out_tokens.reshape(-1), accept_index, W-1). W = verify_num_draft_tokens
  (DSpark) / block_size (DFlash).
- Convention: reported logprob = UN-renormalized log_softmax(logits/temp)
  (matches non-spec sampler and trainer full-vocab recompute; the top-k/p
  renorm in dflash_utils is acceptance-only). With active top-k/top-p
  truncation the reported logprob deliberately differs from the truncated
  sampling distribution.
- GPU-VALIDATE: DSpark greedy spec-on-vs-off tolerance check, non-greedy
  temp!=1/top_p<1, full-vocab recompute reference, folded-path
  (epilogue.strided_logits) population on graph replay. DFLASH-proper
  path shares the code, not yet validated.
